                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "simplex",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "917d2762-6dda-3697-a75a-db53f080bf37",
                                        "entry_id": "b462fbe8-07e3-3514-9fa6-a6729cc70791",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A generalization of a triangle or tetrahedron to an arbitrary dimension, the generalization being the simplest possible convex polytope for a given dimension; more accurately, the convex hull of n+1 affinely independent points in n-dimensional space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1eaf940f-4b1b-38ef-ba4e-198b3f1d85cb",
                                        "entry_id": "b462fbe8-07e3-3514-9fa6-a6729cc70791",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A word which is not compound and contains no derivational affixes (inflectional affixes are usually disregarded); a monomorphemic word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f92cc43-4409-4ef7-96f7-a716a1df148c",
                                                "sense_id": "1eaf940f-4b1b-38ef-ba4e-198b3f1d85cb",
                                                "text": "The word weak is a simplex. Its derivative weaken is not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35a02232-a8d2-3654-b0cd-e2903529ec9c",
                                        "entry_id": "b462fbe8-07e3-3514-9fa6-a6729cc70791",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In full simplex sentence: in transformational grammar: a simple sentence which is the product of a few transformations; a kernel sentence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63f989dd-e472-419c-ac00-2eb4a04d7021",
                                                "sense_id": "35a02232-a8d2-3654-b0cd-e2903529ec9c",
                                                "text": "The question is: is 139. [“Priexal Vanja. ‘arrived Vanya’”] a simplex or is it a cleft structure in which all 'superfluous' constituents were deleted. […] The only indication that 139. is a simplex is the sentence intonation and the absence of a break between the verb and the subject."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8caf4d5c-bcd7-3c90-98d1-e2ed01d45adb",
                                        "entry_id": "b462fbe8-07e3-3514-9fa6-a6729cc70791",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An apartment (or, sometimes, another type of property) having only one floor or storey; a single-storey property."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
